        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nervous System",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DEEP STRUCTURES:\n  Basal ganglia (striatum, globus pallidus, substantia nigra, STN)\n    → movement initiation and suppression, habit formation\n  Thalamus: relay station — almost all sensory info passes through\n    (except olfaction → goes direct to cortex)\n  Hypothalamus: master homeostasis controller + circadian clock (SCN)\n    + appetite (arcuate nucleus), temperature, osmoregulation\n  Limbic system: emotion + memory\n    Amygdala: threat detection, fear conditioning, emotional salience\n    Hippocampus: spatial maps, episodic memory encoding\n    Cingulate cortex: conflict monitoring, pain affect, social cognition"
    }
